  "note": "Named assignments the play designs refer to by id (designed, not fitted; docs/specs/m3-playbook-and-custom-routes.md, milestone A). Waypoints are [lateral, up] in yards. 'up' is upfield for the offense, so a rush or a blitz has falling values. The waypoints are measured from the player's own alignment, with two exceptions: a runPath is measured from the ball, [toward the play side, past the line], and a block on the 'hole' axis from the design's hole, the spot where its run path crosses the line, [outside the hole, past the line], so lead and pulling blockers always arrive where the runner goes. The lateral axis: 'in' is toward the middle of the field (a player on the middle goes to the offense's right), 'side' is toward the side the design names with `to`, 'none' means the entry has no lateral move. A man entry covers the first listed spot the formation has, and plays its fallback against a formation with none of them. A route's family and direction are what the classifier must return for it (criterion B3); breakAt is the index of the waypoint a design's `depth` places: the break, or the end of a route that ends vertical. `depth` moves that waypoint and every later one so it sits that many yards past the line. Where the route is caught follows from its family (data/plays/config.json classifier.catchAtEnd). A zone entry has no waypoints: the design gives the landmark with `at`. Routes whose shapes come from data/ui/templates.json keep those waypoints.",
